in case you didn't know at least one of  the endings of eldon ring the one i  defended in my which ending his best  video the age of the stars has some  serious mistranslations which might  affect its meaning and lore implications  an article released two weeks ago from  frontline jp that claimed the dialogue  spoken by ronnie in the ending along  with her final voice lines at her rise  were mistranslations there were a few  videos released reporting on the article  and i've gotten an unending stream of  comments just letting me know that  actually the ending was mistranslated  whenever it comes up in one of my videos  so in this video i want to talk about  the mistranslations and what they mean  for the lore and our understanding of  the ending  first i haven't discussed the  mistranslations yet because i was  working on other videos and because i  wanted to verify the potential  mistranslations before i mindlessly  reported on them fortunately i have two  genuine native japanese speaking friends  who are nice enough to take some time to  review the article and the  mistranslation claims they have both  confirmed that the article is pretty  much correct and the english text and  voice lines are basically  mistranslations  the main thrust of difference between  the english and the original japanese is  that the english is both more obscure  and contorts a lot of the japanese  meaning i already explained the english  in my previous video so i'll just  summarize the japanese here  unlike the english the japanese ending  dialogue says that the chill night is  not beginning but will be kept far away  and the journey of loneliness on the  dark path is a personal one for ronnie  and maybe us as the tarnished as well to  go on to keep the knight far away not  one that everyone will be going on the  dialogue in ronnie's room explains this  more the order is what ronnie wants to  keep far away she may think that it is  impossible to destroy the order without  also destroying lives and souls this is  a thought that could be supported by  what i talked about in the outer gods  video that the greater will was  responsible for creating individuals and  lives and souls its order cannot be  destroyed without also destroying its  effects individuals and lives and so  forth so the order may be needed but  ronnie thinks it would be better if it  were far away where people couldn't  touch or clearly see it maybe so that  they would not be directly influenced by  it  the english took ronnie's words about  not being able to touch or clearly see  it to be a lot stronger than they were  in the japanese where she is simply  suggesting that it might be better that  way and that she is talking about the  order not simply the senses themselves  the article concludes succinctly  summarizing the actual state of things  it says  ronnie believes that while the order may  have to exist as it is entwined with  life and souls it causes problems for  the people her solution is thus to take  it and leave keeping it far away where  people cannot see feel touch and believe  in it embarking on a journey into fear  doubt solitude and darkness to do so  so there we have the updated ending and  to be fair it seems pretty clear now we  might ask how should we view the ending  differently well i have two answers to  this first i don't think this really  changes much thematically from my  original interpretation sure there's a  change in that ronnie didn't destroy the  order but the idea of removing influence  from outside forces and letting people  live their own individual lives was the  central theme i took out of the ending  before and that is basically the  takeaway of the japanese lines as well  i know a good amount of people took the  ending in english to be pretty ominous  but this should probably put those fears  to rest  this really only strengthens my previous  case that the age of the stars ending is  the best one giving freedom and  individuality to people by taking an  actually meaningful action to change the  current status quo  obviously this is still my previous line  of argumentation so if you haven't seen  my which ending is best video that will  explain things in more detail even  though that's working off of  mistranslations but as i said doesn't  seem like the mistranslations change the  theme very much at least from what i  took from it before my second answer to  how this should impact our view of the  ending is basically i don't care the  version of the game that essentially  every english player plays is the one  with the mistranslations mistranslations  that got all the way from dialogue and  descriptions to the actual voice lines  of dialogue i remind you that the  english voice lines are the only voice  lines recorded for eldon ring there are  no original voice japanese lines the  dialogue is english only i mean yeah  it's cool to see what was actually  intended by fromsoft and it does seem to  be more straightforward and make easier  sense but also my experience with the  game is with the descriptions i read and  the dialogue i hear the tones and themes  still shone through the same at least  they did to me and that is really the  most important part it's also a part  that oftentimes does not really need  deep lore speculation to reach so yeah i  don't care that much about the  mistranslations it's cool to get the  original text but the game in english  has become a bit of its own beast and  players will treat it as such at least  until fromsoft decides to fix the  mistranslations which i'd say has about  a 0.1 percent chance of happening this  might be a very unusual case of death of  the author  for better or for worse the english game  stands on its own and i think that's at  least neutral since the themes read  similarly to me so really i don't think  it's something to sweat that much  yeah it might be mistranslated but the  story and its culmination still stand in  the same place in all their lore based  splendor and ronnie ii still remains  based  there are of course more questions about  the moon ronnie's connections and plenty  more lore of the lands between so if you  want to see here and explore more of  that you should subscribe as i'll be  making more excursions into the lore on  my channel i hope you enjoyed watching  and feel free to leave a comment about  your thoughts on the mistranslation and  what it means to you again thanks for  watching bye
 

